---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import OverlapChecker from '../components/OverlapChecker.astro';
import NavBar from '../components/NavBar.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Subnet Overlap Checker – CIDR Conflict Detector | DevSubnet"
  description="Subnet overlap checker detecting identical, overlapping, and contained CIDR ranges. Essential before VPC peering, VPN routing, firewall changes, and infrastructure deployments to prevent ambiguous routing and traffic loss."
>
  <div class="app-shell">
    <NavBar path="overlap" />
    <main>
      <section class="intro" aria-labelledby="page-title">
        <div class="eyebrow">CONFLICT DETECTION / CIDR OVERLAP CHECKER</div>
        <h1 id="page-title">Subnet Overlap Checker</h1>
        <p class="lede">Compare multiple CIDR blocks to identify identical, overlapping, contained, and separate relationships — essential before VPC peering, VPN, firewall, and routing changes.</p>
      </section>
      <section aria-label="Overlap checker workspace">
        <OverlapChecker />
      </section>
      <section class="guide-section">
        <div class="guide-sticky"><h2>Why check for <em>overlaps</em>?</h2></div>
        <div class="guide-content">
          <div class="guide-block">
            <h3>The cost of overlapping subnets</h3>
            <p>Overlapping ranges break VPC peering, VPN routing, and on-prem integrations. A single address existing in two networks creates ambiguous routing decisions and can silently drop or misroute traffic. Detecting overlap before deployment avoids expensive fixes later.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="guide-block">
            <h3>Common conflict types</h3>
            <p><strong>Identical</strong> ranges are exactly the same prefix. <strong>Contained</strong> networks sit fully inside a larger block (e.g. 192.168.1.128/25 inside 192.168.1.0/24). <strong>Overlapping</strong> networks share only part of their address space. Use the checker to confirm a change is safe before you commit.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="guide-block">
            <h3>Related Tools</h3>
            <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 1rem;">
              <li><a href="/" style="color: var(--text-primary); text-decoration: none;">IPv4 Subnet Calculator</a></li>
              <li><a href="/visual-subnet-splitter" style="color: var(--text-primary); text-decoration: none;">Visual Subnet Splitter</a></li>
              <li><a href="/vlsm-calculator" style="color: var(--text-primary); text-decoration: none;">VLSM Calculator</a></li>
              <li><a href="/cidr-cheat-sheet" style="color: var(--text-primary); text-decoration: none;">CIDR Cheat Sheet</a></li>
              <li><a href="/cidr-supernet-calculator" style="color: var(--text-primary); text-decoration: none;">Supernetter</a></li>
              <li><a href="/kubernetes-subnet-planner" style="color: var(--text-primary); text-decoration: none;">K8s Planner</a></li>
              <li><a href="/terraform-subnet-planner" style="color: var(--text-primary); text-decoration: none;">Terraform Planner</a></li>
              <li><a href="/aws-vpc-subnet-calculator" style="color: var(--text-primary); text-decoration: none;">AWS VPC Calc</a></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
    <footer>
      <span>DEVSUBNET.COM / ENGINEERED FOR CLEAR NETWORKS</span>
      <div class="footer-links"><a href="/about">About Us</a><a href="/contact">Contact</a><a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a><a href="/terms">Terms</a><a href="/faq">FAQ</a></div>
      <span>NO DATA LEAVES YOUR DEVICE</span>
    </footer>
  </div>
</Layout>
